agm: 1.0
package: api.patterns
version: 0.2.0
title: API Anti-Pattern Catalogue

node api.anti_pattern.god_endpoint
type: anti_pattern
summary: do not create single endpoints that handle many unrelated operations via a type parameter
priority: high
stability: high
detail:
  A god endpoint accepts a generic action field and routes to unrelated logic
  internally. This pattern defeats HTTP semantics, makes authorization complex,
  and creates hidden coupling between unrelated features.

  Bad:
    POST /api/action with body containing a type field dispatching to unrelated logic

  Good:
    POST /api/users
    DELETE /api/invoices/{id}
    POST /api/reports/run
resolution:
  Split into separate, purpose-specific endpoints. Use HTTP methods to express
  the intent (POST for creation, PUT/PATCH for updates, DELETE for removal).
